        """
        This function compares image vs golden image stored in SVN.

        :param params: Dictionary with these keys:
                        'image': REQUIRED str. Must be one of the keys in DisplayConstant.image_compare_items, for
                        example 'ACTIVE FAULTS: NONE', 'F1_DOWN', or 'System Configuration-Locomotive Specifications'.
                        The constant entry supplies image TYPE, ID, coordinates, and optionally OCR fields such as
                        expected_text, filter, bg_color, text_color, language, oem, and psm.
                        'Control_Value': OPTIONAL str deprecated alias. If present, the code replaces 'image' with
                        this value after the initial 'image' lookup. 'image' is still required; prefer 'image' only.
                        'ctrl_existance': OPTIONAL bool. Default is True. This misspelled key name is required by the
                        code. False means the control/image is not expected to exist.
                        'time_out': OPTIONAL int | str seconds. Default is 20 when EXECUTION_TYPE is 'Manual';
                        otherwise default is 60. Values are converted with int().
                        'Position': OPTIONAL int 1-based position. When greater than 1, moves the image coordinate by
                        Offset * (Position - 1). Default is no movement.
                        'Offset': OPTIONAL int | float pixel distance for 'Position'. Default is 80.
                        'offset_direction': OPTIONAL Literal['VERTICAL', 'HORIZONTAL']. Exact uppercase is required;
                        the value is not case-normalized. Default is 'HORIZONTAL'. 'VERTICAL' moves y, 'HORIZONTAL'
                        moves x.
                        'expected_bool': OPTIONAL bool. Default is True. True expects the captured image/OCR text to
                        match; False expects it not to match.
                        'expected_result': OPTIONAL bool | Literal['DISPLAYED', 'NOT_DISPLAYED']. String values are
                        exact uppercase and are not case-normalized. 'NOT_DISPLAYED' sets 'expected_bool' to False for
                        script calls. String values can make the return value 'DISPLAYED' or 'NOT_DISPLAYED'. Int
                        values are converted to bool with a warning.
                        'CDU2': OPTIONAL bool | Literal['True', 'False']. String values are exact-case. True or 'True'
                        uses CDU_TRIPLEX2; False, 'False', or omission uses CDU_TRIPLEX.
                        'coordinate': OPTIONAL str. If this value contains the lowercase substring 'dynamic',
                        compare_image calls verify_scr_text to scan screen text dynamically instead of doing the
                        normal image compare. The 'image' constant must provide expected_text for this mode.
                        'quarter': OPTIONAL list[int] used only with dynamic 'coordinate'. Default is [1, 2, 3, 4].
                        'size': OPTIONAL int used only with dynamic 'coordinate' as coordinate height. Default is 15.
                        'is_coord': OPTIONAL marker of any value forwarded to verify_image_text when the 'image'
                        constant has expected_text. If present, params itself supplies the OCR control definition
                        instead of DisplayConstant.image_compare_items['image']; also supply 'coordinate' and
                        'expected_text' as described below.
                        'expected_text': CONDITIONALLY REQUIRED dict[str, str] when 'is_coord' is present. In normal
                        mode this is read from DisplayConstant.image_compare_items['image']['expected_text'], not from
                        params.
                        'filter': OPTIONAL filter class | dict with 'is_coord'. Default in verify_image_text is
                        BasicFilter. Common values are BasicFilter, ResizeFilter, MorphologyFilter, and
                        ResizeMorphologyFilter.
                        'bg_color': OPTIONAL dict[str, str | list[str]] with 'is_coord'. Values should be color names
                        from DisplayConstant.Color_Hash_Table, for example 'WHITE', 'BLACK', 'RED', 'YELLOW', or
                        'CYAN'.
                        'text_color': OPTIONAL dict[str, str | list[str]] with 'is_coord'. Use color names from
                        DisplayConstant.Color_Hash_Table.
                        'language': OPTIONAL str with 'is_coord'. OCR language/traineddata name such as 'eng',
                        'wabtec_OBdiag2', 'fra', or 'por'. Default is None.
                        'oem': OPTIONAL int OCR engine mode forwarded to verify_image_text. Default is 3.
                        'psm': OPTIONAL int OCR page segmentation mode forwarded to verify_image_text. Default is 3.
                        'remove_selection': OPTIONAL bool forwarded to the image filter. Default is False.
                        'condition': OPTIONAL str forwarded to verify_image_text for expected_text expressions, for
